# SPA fallback for Cloudflare Pages (and Netlify, same syntax).
#
# web.output is "single", so the export produces ONE index.html and every route
# is resolved client-side by Expo Router. Without this rule a hard load or a
# refresh on any path other than "/" — /readings/face, /astrology/daily, a push
# notification deep link, a bookmarked page — returns the host's 404.
#
# It is not only a routing nicety: the service worker refreshes its offline
# shell from navigation responses, so a 404 here would be a 404 cached as the
# app. sw.js guards that too (it only stores a successful response), and the two
# defences are deliberately independent.
#
# 200 = rewrite, not redirect: the URL the user sees is preserved, which is what
# lets the router read the path on boot.
/*    /index.html   200
